WHAT SEPARATES, AND WHAT DOES NOT:
  Gauss(true)      rounding at every skewness and every shape. The
                   identity sum_f C_f (x) S_f = V I is why, and it was
                   measured to 2.9e-16 over 20000 tetrahedra
  Gauss(interp)    exact at skewness 0; O(1) or worse at any non-zero
                   skewness. The sliver column is larger than the
                   well-shaped one, so SHAPE AMPLIFIES what SKEWNESS
                   causes -- two causes, and only the first is a mesh
                   quality question P19-VALID-001 owns
  least-squares    rounding throughout, by construction: it fits the
                   neighbour values at their own centroids and
                   interpolates nothing
  the eigenvalue   finite but large. Four neighbours in three unknowns
  ratio            is barely over-determined, so a CONDITIONING GATE is
                   a requirement and not a refinement
